          "en": "| | Symmetric encryption | Asymmetric encryption | Hashing |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Keys | **One** shared secret key | **A pair**: public key + private key | **No** key |\n| Reversible? | Yes, with the same key | Yes, with the other key of the pair | **No**, one-way |\n| Speed | Very fast (GB/s) | Slow (100 to 1000 times slower) | Very fast |\n| Current algorithms | AES-256-GCM, ChaCha20-Poly1305 | RSA (3072 bits and more), ECDSA, Ed25519, X25519 | SHA-256, SHA-3, BLAKE2 |\n| Avoid | DES, 3DES, RC4, AES in ECB mode | 1024-bit RSA, DSA | MD5, SHA-1 |\n| Typical use | Encrypting files, disks, databases, TLS traffic | Exchanging a key, signing, proving an identity | Checking integrity, fingerprint of a file |\n| Main difficulty | Getting the key to the other side without interception | Slowness, limited message size | Does not provide confidentiality |\n\nCryptography serves four goals: **confidentiality** (nobody else can read), **integrity** (nobody\nchanged it), **authenticity** (the message really comes from the right party) and\n**non-repudiation** (the author cannot deny it). No single family covers them all: that is why\nthey are combined.\n"
